---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy — Checkers"
  description="Privacy Policy for the Checkers application developed by developedbyjacob."
>
  <section class="pt-28 pb-16 md:pt-32 md:pb-24">
    <div class="container-app max-w-3xl">
      <a
        href="/"
        class="inline-flex items-center gap-1 text-sm text-gray-500 dark:text-gray-400 hover:text-accent-600 dark:hover:text-accent-400 transition-colors mb-8"
      >
        <svg class="w-4 h-4" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2">
          <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M15 19l-7-7 7-7" />
        </svg>
        Back to portfolio
      </a>

      <span class="text-accent-600 dark:text-accent-400 font-mono text-xs tracking-widest uppercase notranslate">
        Legal
      </span>
      <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl md:text-5xl font-bold mt-2 mb-4">
        Privacy Policy
      </h1>
      <p class="text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400 mb-2">
        <span class="notranslate">Checkers</span>
      </p>
      <p class="text-sm text-gray-500 dark:text-gray-500 notranslate">
        Last updated: September 30, 2026
      </p>

      <div class="prose-policy mt-10 space-y-8 text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300 leading-relaxed">
        <p>
          This Privacy Policy explains how <span class="notranslate">developedbyjacob</span>
          handles information related to the use of the
          <span class="notranslate">Checkers</span> application (also published as
          <span class="notranslate">Damas</span>, <span class="notranslate">Dama</span>,
          <span class="notranslate">Damenspiel</span>, <span class="notranslate">Jeu de Dames</span>,
          <span class="notranslate">Warcaby</span> and <span class="notranslate">Dam</span>
          depending on the device language), hereinafter the "Application".
        </p>
        <p>By using the Application, the user accepts the practices described in this Privacy Policy.</p>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white mb-3">1. Application controller</h2>
          <p>Developer: <span class="notranslate">developedbyjacob</span></p>
          <p>Contact email: <a href="mailto:kiktruedeveloper@gmail.com" class="text-accent-700 dark:text-accent-400 hover:underline notranslate">kiktruedeveloper@gmail.com</a></p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white mb-3">2. Information stored in the Application</h2>
          <p>The Application is a checkers (draughts) game that allows users to play against another person on the same device or against the computer, using Spanish, International, or American rules. The Application does not require an account and does not ask for names, email addresses, or any other personal details. To provide its features, the Application stores the following information locally on the device:</p>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-6 mt-3 space-y-1">
            <li>User preferences: selected rule set and selected board theme.</li>
            <li>Completed games counter, used only to decide how often interstitial ads are shown.</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="mt-3">The game in progress is kept only while the Application is running and is not permanently saved. Games against the computer are calculated entirely on the device.</p>
          <p class="mt-3">This information is stored locally on the user's device and is not sent to servers operated by the developer. The developer cannot access, view, or retrieve the data saved by the user.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white mb-3">3. Language and default rules</h2>
          <p>The Application is displayed in the language of the device. The default rule set (Spanish, International, or American) is chosen on the device according to the device's language and region settings. This choice is made locally and is not sent to the developer. The user can change the rule set at any time, and the selected option is stored locally on the device.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white mb-3">4. Permissions</h2>
          <p>The Application requests the following Android permissions:</p>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-6 mt-3 space-y-1">
            <li><code class="notranslate">INTERNET</code>: required to load advertisements, show the consent message, and check for Application updates.</li>
            <li><code class="notranslate">ACCESS_NETWORK_STATE</code>: used by the Google Mobile Ads SDK to detect whether a network connection is available.</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="mt-3">The game itself can be played without an internet connection.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white mb-3">5. Advertising through Google AdMob</h2>
          <p>The Application displays banner and interstitial advertisements through <span class="notranslate">Google AdMob</span>, a service provided by Google. Interstitial advertisements are shown only occasionally, after a game has finished and the user leaves the results screen.</p>
          <p class="mt-3">The Google Mobile Ads SDK may automatically collect and share certain information, such as:</p>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-6 mt-3 space-y-1">
            <li>IP address, which may be used to estimate the device's general location.</li>
            <li>Device or advertising identifiers, such as the Android Advertising ID or App Set ID.</li>
            <li>Information about interactions with the Application and advertisements (impressions, clicks, video views).</li>
            <li>Diagnostic and performance information, such as errors, startup times, or SDK operation.</li>
            <li>Technical information about the device, operating system, and Application.</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="mt-3">Google may use this information to show advertisements, measure their performance, perform analytics, limit their frequency, and prevent fraud or misuse. Depending on the user's location, settings, and consent, advertisements may be personalized or non-personalized.</p>
          <p class="mt-3">Information processed by Google is subject to Google's terms and privacy policies, including the <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-accent-700 dark:text-accent-400 hover:underline">Google Privacy Policy</a> and <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-accent-700 dark:text-accent-400 hover:underline">how Google uses information from sites or apps that use its services</a>. The user can view and change advertising preferences in the privacy and advertising settings of their Google account or Android device.</p>
          <p class="mt-3">Game data and user preferences are not deliberately sent to Google AdMob to personalize advertisements.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white mb-3">6. Advertising consent</h2>
          <p>In territories where legally required, such as the European Economic Area, the United Kingdom, and Switzerland, the Application displays a consent message through Google's User Messaging Platform (UMP) allowing the user to manage their privacy and advertising preferences. Advertisements are only requested after this consent process has been completed.</p>
          <p class="mt-3">The user may accept, reject, or modify certain options related to the use of data for personalized advertising, according to the options available in Google's consent message. Where applicable, the user can review or change these choices at any time from the "Privacy options" link on the main menu of the Application.</p>
          <p class="mt-3">Withdrawing consent does not necessarily prevent advertisements from being shown, but they may be non-personalized or subject to more limited data processing.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white mb-3">7. Application updates</h2>
          <p>The Application uses the Google Play In-App Updates service to check whether a newer version is available on Google Play and, if so, to offer the user the option to download it. This check is performed by Google Play and is subject to Google's privacy policies. The developer does not receive any information from this process.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white mb-3">8. Purpose of processing</h2>
          <p>The information described in this Policy is used to:</p>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-6 mt-3 space-y-1">
            <li>Provide the core checkers gameplay features, including games against the computer.</li>
            <li>Apply user preferences (rule set and board theme).</li>
            <li>Display and measure advertisements through Google AdMob and control how often interstitial ads appear.</li>
            <li>Request and manage advertising consent where legally required.</li>
            <li>Offer Application updates through Google Play.</li>
            <li>Maintain the security, stability, and operation of the Application.</li>
            <li>Prevent fraud and misuse related to advertising.</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="mt-3">Game data and preferences are not sold or used by the developer for external commercial purposes.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white mb-3">9. Data retention and deletion</h2>
          <p>Locally stored preferences and the completed games counter remain on the device until the user:</p>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-6 mt-3 space-y-1">
            <li>Clears the Application's data in Android settings.</li>
            <li>Uninstalls the Application.</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="mt-3">Because the developer does not receive or store this data on its own servers, it cannot delete it remotely or recover it after it has been deleted. Data processed by Google AdMob is retained according to the policies and periods established by Google.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white mb-3">10. Security</h2>
          <p>The Application uses the storage and security mechanisms provided by Android. However, no electronic system can guarantee absolute security. Users are advised to protect their device with a password, PIN, pattern, fingerprint, or another locking method.</p>
          <p class="mt-3">Data transmitted by the Google Mobile Ads SDK, the User Messaging Platform, and Google Play services is sent over encrypted connections.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white mb-3">11. Children</h2>
          <p>The Application is not specifically designed for children and does not knowingly seek to collect personal information from minors. Google AdMob is configured so that advertisements do not exceed a content rating suitable for teenagers.</p>
          <p class="mt-3">If a parent or guardian believes that a minor has improperly provided personal information, they may contact the developer using the email address indicated in this Policy.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white mb-3">12. Third-party services</h2>
          <p>The Application may interact with external services, mainly:</p>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-6 mt-3 space-y-1">
            <li>Google AdMob (advertising).</li>
            <li>Google User Messaging Platform (consent management).</li>
            <li>Google Play In-App Updates (update checks).</li>
            <li>Android system services for storage.</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="mt-3">Processing performed by these services is governed by their own privacy policies and terms of use.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white mb-3">13. User rights and control</h2>
          <p>The user retains control over the data stored on their device and can modify or delete it from the Application or the Android system settings.</p>
          <p class="mt-3">The user can also:</p>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-6 mt-3 space-y-1">
            <li>Review or change advertising consent from the "Privacy options" link in the main menu, where available.</li>
            <li>Reset or delete the advertising identifier in the device's privacy settings.</li>
            <li>Manage Google advertising and privacy preferences in <a href="https://adssettings.google.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-accent-700 dark:text-accent-400 hover:underline">Google Ads Settings</a>.</li>
            <li>Clear the Application's data in Android settings.</li>
            <li>Uninstall the Application.</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="mt-3">For any privacy-related questions, the user can contact the developer at <a href="mailto:kiktruedeveloper@gmail.com" class="text-accent-700 dark:text-accent-400 hover:underline notranslate">kiktruedeveloper@gmail.com</a>.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white mb-3">14. Changes to this Privacy Policy</h2>
          <p>This Privacy Policy may be updated when new features, external services, or legal changes are introduced. The date of the last update will appear at the beginning of the document. Users are advised to review this Policy periodically to learn about any changes.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white mb-3">15. Contact</h2>
          <p>For questions, requests, or concerns related to this Privacy Policy, you can use the following email address:</p>
          <p class="mt-3">
            <a href="mailto:kiktruedeveloper@gmail.com" class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 text-accent-700 dark:text-accent-400 hover:underline font-medium notranslate">
              <svg class="w-4 h-4" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2">
                <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M3 8l7.89 5.26a2 2 0 002.22 0L21 8M5 19h14a2 2 0 002-2V7a2 2 0 00-2-2H5a2 2 0 00-2 2v10a2 2 0 002 2z" />
              </svg>
              kiktruedeveloper@gmail.com
            </a>
          </p>
        </section>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
